answer.worked:
The circumference of the disc is:
$$\begin{align*}
C &= 2\pi r = 2\pi \times 5 = 10\pi \text{ cm}
\end{align*}$$
At 10 revolutions per minute, the distance travelled per minute by a point on the circumference is:
$$\begin{align*}
v &= 10 \times 10\pi \\
&= 100\pi \text{ cm min}^{-1}
\end{align*}$$
Correct answer: C.

The front edge consists of two arcs and the straight length $AD$.
$$\begin{align*}
EADF &= 2 \times 22 \times \frac{\pi}{5} + 72 \\
&\approx 99.64601535 \\
&\approx 99.65\text{ m}
\end{align*}$$

