answer.worked:
Let the radius of the circle be $r = OX = OZ$.
$$\begin{align*}
\text{Area of minor sector} &= \frac{1}{2}r^2\theta \\
12\pi &= \frac{1}{2}r^2\left(\frac{2\pi}{3}\right) \\
12\pi &= \frac{\pi}{3}r^2 \\
r^2 &= 36 \\
r &= 6 \text{ cm}
\end{align*}$$
The angle of the major sector (shaded region) is $2\pi - \frac{2\pi}{3} = \frac{4\pi}{3}$.
$$\begin{align*}
\text{Arc length of shaded region} &= r\theta_{\text{major}} \\
&= 6 \times \frac{4\pi}{3} \\
&= 8\pi \text{ cm}
\end{align*}$$
The perimeter of the shaded region includes the major arc and the two radii:
$$\begin{align*}
\text{Perimeter} &= OX + OZ + \text{arc length} \\
&= 6 + 6 + 8\pi \\
&= 12 + 8\pi \text{ cm}
\end{align*}$$

